# Googlebook OS on SM-T870: the tablet's camera provider with the camera orientation re-expressed
# for the landscape natural orientation (T870-araclar/dogal-yon/hal, yamalar/dogal_yon_hal.py).
#
# It replaces the LineageOS vendor service vendor.camera.provider
# (/vendor/etc/init/android.hardware.camera.provider-service.samsung.rc) the way the sensors HAL
# and pil-sagligi's health HAL do: an "override" across the treble boundary is refused by init
# (system/core/init/service_parser.cpp EndSection), so the vendor service is stopped before its
# class starts and this one serves ICameraProvider/internal/0 with the same class, user, groups,
# I/O priority, capabilities and task profiles.
#
# The vendor service keeps its "interface aidl ...ICameraProvider/internal/0" line; init allows
# only one service per interface (service_parser.cpp ParseInterface), so this one has none.

on early-init
    stop vendor.camera.provider

service gbos.camera.provider /product/bin/hw/android.hardware.camera.provider-service.samsung-gbos
    class hal
    user cameraserver
    group audio camera input drmrpc usb
    ioprio rt 4
    capabilities SYS_NICE
    task_profiles CameraServiceCapacity MaxPerformance

# vndservicemanager restarts the whole hal class when it restarts ("onrestart class_restart hal",
# without --only-enabled), which starts the stopped vendor service too. Because the vendor service
# declares the interface, servicemanager would also start it on demand (ctl.interface_start) for a
# client waiting for ICameraProvider/internal/0; cameraserver only waits like that for a lazy
# provider (ro.camera.enableLazyHal, not set on this device: AidlProviderInfo::
# startProviderInterface), otherwise it uses checkService and registration notifications. Either
# way the vendor service is stopped again and this one registers anew.
on property:init.svc.vendor.camera.provider=running
    stop vendor.camera.provider
    restart gbos.camera.provider
